      "title": "Books & Publications",
      "content": "<h1>Books &amp; Publications</h1>\n<h2>My ML Engineering Book</h2>\n<h3>\"Production Machine Learning Systems\"</h3>\n<p><em>A comprehensive guide to building scalable ML systems</em></p>\n<p><strong>Status:</strong> In Progress | <strong>Expected:</strong> 2024</p>\n<p>This book covers the complete ML lifecycle from research to production, including:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Model development and experimentation</li>\n<li>MLOps and deployment strategies  </li>\n<li>Monitoring and maintenance</li>\n<li>Scaling considerations</li>\n</ul>\n<p><a href=\"/pdfs/sample-chapter.pdf\">Read Sample Chapter (PDF)</a> | <a href=\"https://github.com/yourusername/ml-book\">GitHub Repository</a></p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Recommended Reading</h2>\n<h3>Essential ML Books</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>\"Designing Machine Learning Systems\"</strong> by Chip Huyen</li>\n<li><strong>\"Machine Learning Design Patterns\"</strong> by Lakshmanan, Robinson &amp; Munn</li>\n<li><strong>\"Building Machine Learning Powered Applications\"</strong> by Emmanuel Ameisen</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Papers I'm Reading</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762\">Attention Is All You Need</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.04805\">BERT: Pre-training of Deep Bidirectional Transformers</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.14165\">GPT-3: Language Models are Few-Shot Learners</a></li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>Book Reviews &amp; Notes</h2>\n<p>I regularly review ML books and papers. Check out my <a href=\"https://notion.so/yourworkspace/reading-notes\">Notion reading notes</a> for detailed summaries and insights.</p>",
